    {
      "id": "be8c6e1226342b2d14e851300a6a33922aa746e6",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1130692726,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Well, that's a crock.\n\nPerhaps when the TRANSUM plugin was originally written, \"tcp.analysis.retransmission\" and \"tcp.analysis.keep_alive\" were Boolean fields rather than expert infos, but they're expert infos now (and maybe they always were), so they don't have values - they're either present or absent, and that's it.\n\nWe weren't making sure that we were trying to fetch the value of a Boolean field until this change; now that we are, it managed to find this bug in the TRANSUM code. !8473 changes the TRANSUM code to check whether those fields are present rather than checking their non-existent value (which, before the check was done, probably returned either random values or always-false values).",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-10-10T23:05:56.862Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-10-11T00:03:46.295Z",
